      "content": "but they don't see me like that. they see the grades, the awards, the \"success.\" that's the only version of me that actually exists to them. if that version is dead, then there's nothing left to show them. it feels like i'm just dragging out the inevitable shame. wouldn't it be easier for everyone if the memory of who i was stayed perfect, instead of watching me slowly fall apart and fail at everything else?",
